{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"choosy-arthrodic-barbet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n`_compact_on_close` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`) takes the ONE tickets write\nlock and holds it for MINUTES on a large store, at the very end of every close. This is the\nactual source of the \"long-lasting locks on the tickets branch\" reported against the close\npath — not the LLM completion verifier, which has always run outside the lock.\n\n## Evidence (this host, tracker 745M / ~4000 ticket dirs)\nLive capture of pid 85578 `rebar transition ethnogenic-centaurian-rat in_progress closed --ref c392d736`:\n- 20:51:46 COMPLETION_VERDICT commit (verifier already done; no lock held)\n- 20:51:54 STATUS commit\n- 20:51:56 SIGNATURE commit\n- 20:51:59 `.ticket-write.lock.d` created, stamp `pid=85578`\n- 20:54:37 COMPACT commit -> lock released\n\n~2m38s of continuous write-lock hold, entirely attributable to compact-on-close. Bug 7084\nmeasured the same holder at 48.1s and added a stand-aside probe; the probe is INEFFECTIVE for\nthe closing process, because that process released the lock microseconds earlier, so\n`write_lock_is_busy` reports \"free\" and compaction takes the lock anyway. Concurrent agents\nthen burn their 60s acquire budget (the REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES work, cc69cc1179, treats that\nsymptom).\n\n## Root-cause direction (to be planned)\nCompaction is OPTIONAL housekeeping (a skip is a correctness no-op — the raw events stay live).\nOptions to evaluate:\n- move compact-on-close off the foreground close entirely (defer to an out-of-band/idle path);\n- bound the lock-held portion (chunk, or do the fold outside the lock and take the lock only for\n  the rename+commit);\n- make the stand-aside guard consider recent contention rather than one instantaneous probe.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A close does not hold the tickets write lock for a duration that scales with store size.\n- [ ] Compaction's correctness is unchanged (a deferred/skipped fold is still picked up later).\n- [ ] Regression test: a close on a store with a large event log does not hold the write lock\n      across the fold (assert lock-dir absence / instrumented hold span, no wall-clock budget).\n- [ ] Concurrent writers are not starved by a close that triggers compaction.","id":"cfcb-a023-09a0-42ad","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"compact-on-close holds the tickets write lock for minutes"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786593341503535001,"uuid":"95ff3c04-65b6-4fd8-b62b-339e15166e46"}